  "result": "I added `click.KeyValue`, and its new tests pass along with the rest of `tests/test_types.py`. I didn't run the full suite.\n\n- **Parsing:** it splits on the first `=`, so `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")` and `a=` gives `(\"a\", \"\")`.\n- **Errors:** input with no `=` or with an empty key (`abc`, `=value`, or an empty string) fails with `'\u2026' is not a valid key=value pair.`\n- **Where it lives:** the class is in `src/click/types.py` and is exported in `src/click/__init__.py`.\n- **Tests:** I added valid and invalid cases to `tests/test_types.py`.\n\nI didn't update `CHANGES.md` or `docs/`, which `CLAUDE.md` asks for on user-visible changes. I also skipped docstrings on `convert` and `__repr__`, to match the neighbouring param types. Say if you want any of that added.",
